  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SALW LAS II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">According to Article 1 of Council Decision (CFSP) 2021/1726 in support of combating the illicit trade in and proliferation of small arms and light weapons in the Member States of the League of Arab States (LAS), the Union will pursue the following objectives: sustainably build the national capacity of LAS Member States to combat the illicit proliferation of small arms and light weapons (SALW), combat terrorism and enhance security in post-conflict situations while fully respecting international human rights standards; sustainably build the regional capacity of the LAS to address the same challenges; strengthen LAS Member States&#xbf; national control over SALW at key stages of their life cycle; enhance the exchange of best practices and lessons learned. In order to achieve the objectives, the Union shall, support actions in the following areas: international SALW transfer control (combating illicit arms flows); identification and disruption of sources of illicit small arms (capacity building for law enforcement agencies); other measures related to small-arms control including stockpile management, control of related supplies and security; disarmament, demobilisation and reintegration; provision of information relevant to illicit SALW and enhanced SALW control.</narrative>
  </description>
